      "notes": "The agent is only part of my setup. Codex works with the actual project files and terminal. Skills are reusable instructions for a particular kind of work, while Markdown keeps the goal and important decisions visible. Git records changes. Worktrees let me try things separately without mixing unfinished changes together. Pixi describes the software environment, and DataLad connects data and code with their history. When I need execution records, duct captures what a command did. These tools give the agent something concrete to act on, and give me something concrete to check. The skill workshop and worktree utilities are linked here if you want to explore them.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/leej3/software-engineer-reborn/tree/main/talk-concepts/06-the-ai-era-development-environment.md",
