      "notes": "This is The Software Engineer Reborn, a talk I prepared for the Williamsburg software community. On the left is the preparation: a Talk Atlas where I can compare possible narratives and follow source notes. On the right is the presentation that came out of that process. Making a tool to think with became part of making the talk. The question I kept coming back to was about my own role. As the machine produces more implementation, I spend more attention on defining the problem, selecting evidence, and deciding which work I can actually stand behind. Both the preparation and the finished slides are public.",
