        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "STAMPED principles",
          "x": 730,
          "y": 646,
          "w": 480,
          "h": 38,
          "size": 24,
          "bold": false,
          "color": "#15716e",
          "link": "https://stamped-principles.org/"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The next talk asks, 'What did we just make?' A figure or a report is only the visible result. The useful object also includes the inputs, code, decisions, and environment needed to inspect it or run it again. Our team's STAMPED principles give us a vocabulary for that package: self-contained, tracked, actionable, modular, portable, ephemeral, and distributable. In plain terms: can I get the pieces, see their history, run the procedure, and recover a useful state somewhere else? This matters beyond science. An AI-generated website, spreadsheet, or presentation also needs enough context for the next person to understand what they have.",
      "sources": [
        "https://research-object-with-ai.pages.dev/",
        "https://github.com/leej3/research-object-with-ai",
        "https://stamped-principles.org/"
      ]
    },
