      "notes": "Orinoco Lite is one example of software I've been working on with agents. Research groups have information about people, projects, publications, and software scattered across many places. Here those things become structured records with explicit relationships. The website and this graph are different views of those records. An editor can propose a change through GitHub so the proposal and its review have a visible history. It builds on the upstream ORINOCO work, with a lighter Git-backed deployment. What interests me is the shared context: people can browse it, software can validate it, and agents can work with a clearer description of what the group knows. The screenshot is saved here, so this example doesn't depend on tonight's Wi-Fi.",
      "sources": [
        "https://github.com/ORINOCO-Lite/orinoco-lite-dev",
        "https://dev.centerforopenneuroscience.org/explore/",
        "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22834595"
      ]
